GNU Unifont
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The screen font is built from GNU Unifont, used under the SIL Open Font
License, Version 1.1.

    Copyright Roman Czyborra, Paul Hardy, and the GNU Unifont authors.

tools/mkfont.py extracts the 8x16 glyphs the kernel needs from the Unifont
.hex distribution into kernel/gfx/font8x16.h at build time. Only the glyph
bitmaps for the code points in use are embedded, not the whole font.

The SIL Open Font License 1.1 is available at
https://openfontlicense.org/ .

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
TLS root authorities
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
kernel/net/authorities.h contains the DER encodings of public certificate
authority certificates. The selection of which authorities to trust
follows the Mozilla CA Certificate Program's included-roots list, whose
trust-store data Mozilla distributes under the Mozilla Public License,
Version 2.0 (https://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/).

The certificates themselves are the public certificates issued by those
authorities (Sectigo, Let's Encrypt / ISRG, DigiCert, GlobalSign, Google
Trust Services, and others named in tools/pki/authorities.txt). They are
factual public data. tools/mkauthorities.sh regenerates the header from
the PEM files under tools/pki/authorities/ and the list in
tools/pki/authorities.txt.

A host under a root not in this list is treated as unverified unless its
authority is added in the machine's settings.
